  "question": "Let $\\vec{a}$ and $\\vec{b}$ be two vectors such that $|\\vec{a}|=3$, $|\\vec{b}|=4$, and their vector sum $\\vec{a}+\\vec{b}$ is perpendicular to $\\vec{a}$. What is $\\vec{a} \\cdot \\vec{b}$?",
  "answeroption": "A",
  "explanation": "If $\\vec{a}+\\vec{b}$ is perpendicular to $\\vec{a}$ then $(\\vec{a}+\\vec{b})\\cdot\\vec{a}=0$.<br /><br />$\\vec{a}\\cdot\\vec{a}+\\vec{a}\\cdot\\vec{b}=0$.<br /><br />$|\\vec{a}|^2+\\vec{a}\\cdot\\vec{b}=0$.<br /><br />$9+\\vec{a}\\cdot\\vec{b}=0$.<br /><br />Thus $\\vec{a}\\cdot\\vec{b}=-9$.",
